    "race": "bramblewyrmling",
    "name": "Bramble Wyrmlings",
    "creatureClass": null,
    "bestiaryClass": "Inkborn",
    "bestiaryDifficulty": "hard",
    "bestiaryOccurrence": "Common",
    "imageUrl": "https://static.tibia.com/images/library/bramblewyrmling.gif",
    "description": "Bramble wyrmlings are small, shy dragons that are said to live in the dense forests of Tibia. Their scales are covered with thorns and leaves, which help them camouflage themselves in their environment. They are closely connected to nature and can communicate with the plants and animals of the forest. They are rather shy creatures that only attack humans if they invade their territory. They are said to be the guardians of the forests, protecting the trees and plants from harm. They are able to heal and protect nature and can even bring plants to life to assist them in battle. In addition, one should be wary of their bite, as it can be poisonous. However, they are little more than a legend, as there are no reliable reports of bramble wyrmling sightings. They seem to appear only in fairy tales and stories.",
    "behaviour": "They cannot be paralysed. Moreover, they are strong against earth, holy and physical damage. On the other hand, they are weak against death and fire damage. These creatures can neither be summoned nor convinced. In addition, they are able to sense invisible creatures.",
