    "imageUrl": "https://static.tibia.com/images/library/cinderwyrmling.gif",
    "description": "Cinder wyrmlings are small but dangerous dragons that are said to inhabit the volcanic regions of Tibia. Their scales are red-hot from the heat, and their breath is a stream of fire and sulfur. They are impetuous and unpredictable creatures that like to set fire to everything in their path. They are resistant to fire and heat and should be approached with extreme caution. It is said that lava flows through their veins and that they sleep in the depths of volcanoes, surrounded by mountains of gold and precious stones. They are said to be greedy and possessive, defending their territory with all their might. However, they are little more than a legend, as there are no reliable reports of cinder wyrmling sightings. They seem to appear only in fairy tales and stories.",
    "behaviour": "They cannot be paralysed. Moreover, they are strong against fire, holy and physical damage. On the other hand, they are weak against earth and ice damage. These creatures can neither be summoned nor convinced. In addition, they are able to sense invisible creatures.",
