    "bestiaryDifficulty": "medium",
    "bestiaryOccurrence": "Rare",
    "imageUrl": "https://static.tibia.com/images/library/honeyelemental.gif",
    "description": "The honey elemental is a creature made entirely of pure and undiluted honey, giving it a sticky and viscous nature. Its body is often moulded into a humanoid shape, though its exact dimensions may vary depending on the amount of honey available. \n\nHoney elementals are born from large enchanted honeycombs in a process known as magical apiculture. The honey is exposed to powerful arcane forces, causing it to transform into sentient beings. The honey elemental never moves far away from its honey combs, as it has a strong and powerful connection to them. As it was born from a magically-enhanced honeycomb, the honey elemental feels an intrinsic attachment to them and considers them to be its nest and dwelling place. This connection is so strong that the honey elemental is compelled to always remain in close proximity to its honey combs, never moving too far away. One of the few reasons why a honey elemental will move a little further away from its combs are cherry drops. They are its favourite treat, and it often seeks them out to devour and consume.",
    "behaviour": "They cannot be paralysed. Moreover, they are strong against death, earth, fire, holy and physical damage. On the other hand, they are weak against energy and ice damage. These creatures can neither be summoned nor convinced. In addition, they are able to sense invisible creatures.",
