    "imageUrl": "https://static.tibia.com/images/library/oozingcarcass.gif",
    "description": "The Oozing Carcasses are wretched beings that were once fervent followers of the blood god. Now reduced to rotting shells, their existence is sustained by the remnants of a twisted, semi-sentient decay. Within their decrepit forms, a murky ichor oozes incessantly, a grotesque manifestation of the unholy influence that has befallen them. These semi-living monstrosities shuffle through the desolate landscapes, their movements accompanied by a nauseating squelching sound. While their minds have been reduced to fragmented memories and impulses, the Oozing Carcasses still retain a flicker of their former loyalty, instinctively drawn to areas of concentrated decay where they gather in macabre communion.",
    "behaviour": "They are immune to agony damage and cannot be paralysed. Moreover, they are strong against death, energy and ice damage. On the other hand, they are weak against earth, fire and holy damage. These creatures can neither be summoned nor convinced. In addition, they are able to sense invisible creatures.",
