    "race": "quaralooter",
    "name": "Quara Looters",
    "creatureClass": null,
    "bestiaryClass": "Aquatic",
    "bestiaryDifficulty": "hard",
    "bestiaryOccurrence": "Common",
    "imageUrl": "https://static.tibia.com/images/library/quaralooter.gif",
    "description": "Quara Looters occupy the lowest rung of Quara society, seen as impure and tainted by their own kind, shunned and reviled, forced to eke out a desperate existence in small, roving bands or by allying themselves with less discerning Quara.\nTheir tragic fate often leads them to serve as expendable shock troops for their Plunderer overlords, who treat them with only a modicum of respect. Quara Looters are a pitiable breed, forever caught in a web of prejudice and exploitation, yet they persevere, driven by the faint hope of finding a better life amidst the darkness. They vent their frustration and pain in fits of violence and senseless cruelty. While bowing only to strength and violence, they will harrass and exploit any creature they consider more weak than themselves.",
    "behaviour": "They are immune to agony and ice damage and cannot be paralysed. Moreover, they are strong against death, fire and holy damage. On the other hand, they are weak against earth and energy damage. These creatures can neither be summoned nor convinced. In addition, they are able to sense invisible creatures.",
